The vast majority of the 'skilled' crowd that I talk to consider the
spell ("create familiar") to be worthless, something that we both
also agree on with regard to the vanilla version of the spell at L6.

It is hard for people to change play habits on short notice.  When you
have played as many games as some of those people have, you tend to
stick with the 'old faithful' mechanics unless there is a demonstrated
need to change; my own educated guess on this is that most people do
exactly what you did and ignore the spell because "it's no good."

Many people do not even understand how the spell works, and think
they'll always get a "domestic" pet.  There is little discussion about
the spell in the past to reference, because in vanilla it's a junk
spell; three magic missiles will do you better.  

The task I have to overcome in many instances with Spork is simple 
inertia, though it's not the type you were thinking of above; it's that 
without getting kicked off the rails forcibly, many people will just do 
what they've always done because "that works".

